The Maretron IPG100 transport and the Maretron proprietary opcode table are implemented
from the CANboat project's documentation (maretron-ipg, canboat.json).

Maretron command definitions (126208-wrapped requests, SSC300 compass commands, TLM100
level-configuration reply, TLM100 product code) are based on the n2k project by Martin
Bjorklund, MIT License, https://github.com/mbj4668/n2k (src/maretron-pgns.yaml,
src/n2k_maretron.erl), and Maretron's public SSC300 user's manual.

The tank-capacity command layout follows signalk-tlm100-config by Krillle (MIT),
https://github.com/Krillle/signalk-tlm100-config, which confirmed it on a TLM100.
Maretron-style switch control follows signalk-n2k-switching by Scott Bender (MIT),
https://github.com/sbender9/signalk-n2k-switching.

